course: dictionary
lesson: 5987
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word is the same, but the meaning changes with the words around it, which is its context. «Meal» is a good example, and the clues in the sentence tell you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «A big python can go months without a meal.» Here the clue is the snake: a meal is the food it eats at one time. Ask yourself what would fit. Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Oatmeal» and «cornmeal» use meal in a different way. Here meal is grain ground into a rough powder, and we never say «a meal» of it. Context stops you from mixing up the two meanings.
fact: A meal is the food you eat at one time, such as breakfast, lunch or dinner.
fact: Meal can also mean the time when you eat, as in meal time.
fact: Meal with no «a» is grain ground into a rough powder, like oatmeal or cornmeal.
fact: Names for meals differ: lunch or dinner at midday, dinner, tea or supper in the evening.
fact: «Make a meal of something» means make it take too long.
exercise: «A big python can go months without a meal.» What does meal mean here? | *The food it eats at one time | The time of day it sleeps | A tasty dish served on a plate | Grain ground into a rough powder
exercise: In «oatmeal», meal means | The food you eat at one time | *Grain ground into a rough powder | A hot dinner | Time to eat
exercise: Three meals a day for a week is how many meals in total? | *21 | 28 | 7 | 14
test: «The best compliments are about things people choose or do: a drawing, a goal, their kindness, their effort, a tasty meal.» In «a tasty meal», what does meal mean? | A place where food is cooked | *The food you eat at one time | The time of day you eat | Grain ground into a rough powder
test: Which phrase uses meal for grain ground into a rough powder? | Three meals a day | *Cornmeal for the cake | A hot meal | Meal time at six o'clock
exam: «Winnie the Pooh only wants the honey, but a real bear ... eats the juicy grubs, which is the meal that really fills it up.» What does meal mean here? | Grain ground into a rough powder | A bowl for honey | *The food eaten at one time | The time of day the bear wakes
